#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3. Replace PUB tuples with a `QuantumProgram` {#step-3-replace-pub-tuples-with-a-quantumprogram}"
msgstr "Paso 3. Reemplazar las tuplas PUB con un `QuantumProgram` {#step-3-replace-pub-tuples-with-a-quantumprogram}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead of passing a list of tuples (PUBs), when using Executor, you build a `QuantumProgram` and append _items_ to it.\n"
msgstr "En lugar de pasar una lista de tuplas (PUBs), cuando usas Executor, creas un `QuantumProgram` y le agregas _elementos_.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A `QuantumProgram` accepts _circuit_ items and _samplex_ items:\n"
msgstr "Un `QuantumProgram` acepta elementos de tipo _circuit_ y _samplex_:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`append_circuit_item`: Appends a `CircuitItem`, which is a circuit and (optionally) its\n"
"parameter values. It is executed as-is, without any randomization. \n"
msgstr ""
"`append_circuit_item`: Agrega un `CircuitItem`, que es un circuito y (opcionalmente) sus\n"
"valores de parámetros. Se ejecuta tal cual, sin ninguna aleatorización. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Use this when you just want to sample a circuit, exactly as Sampler would with a PUB that has no\n"
"  twirling; for example, when submitting a plain sampling job, or when you already manually included any\n"
"  variants you want.\n"
"- `append_samplex_item`: Appends a `samplexItem`, which is a *template circuit* plus a\n"
"  *samplex* that generates randomized parameter sets on the server side. \n"
msgstr ""
"  Usa esto cuando solo quieras muestrear un circuito, exactamente como lo haría Sampler con un PUB que no tiene\n"
"  twirling; por ejemplo, cuando envíes un trabajo de muestreo simple, o cuando ya hayas incluido manualmente cualquier\n"
"  variante que quieras.\n"
"- `append_samplex_item`: Agrega un `samplexItem`, que es un *circuito de plantilla* más un\n"
"  *samplex* que genera conjuntos de parámetros aleatorizados en el lado del servidor. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Use this\n"
"  when you want the circuit's content randomized. The primary case is with \n"
"  twirling (gate or measurement) or noise injection. This capability replaces\n"
"  Sampler's built-in twirling.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Usa esto\n"
"  cuando quieras que el contenido del circuito se aleatorice. El caso principal es con\n"
"  twirling (de puerta o de medición) o inyección de ruido. Esta capacidad reemplaza\n"
"  el twirling integrado de Sampler.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A single `QuantumProgram` can accept both item types; each appended item is executed as an\n"
"independent task and produces its own entry in the results. In general, use `append_circuit_item` when your circuit does not need to be randomized. Otherwise, use `append_samplex_item`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Un solo `QuantumProgram` puede aceptar ambos tipos de elementos; cada elemento agregado se ejecuta como una\n"
"tarea independiente y produce su propia entrada en los resultados. En general, usa `append_circuit_item` cuando tu circuito no necesite aleatorizarse. De lo contrario, usa `append_samplex_item`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The next sections show each in turn: parameterized circuits that use \n"
"`append_circuit_item`, and migrating twirling by using `append_samplex_item`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Las siguientes secciones muestran cada uno por turno: circuitos parametrizados que usan \n"
"`append_circuit_item`, y la migración de twirling usando `append_samplex_item`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the following code examples, `isa_circuit` refers to the circuit that has been transpiled to conform to the target backend's [Instruction Set Architecture](/guides/transpile#instruction-set-architecture) (ISA). This `isa_circuit` contains two parameters.\n"
msgstr "En los siguientes ejemplos de código, `isa_circuit` se refiere al circuito que se ha transpilado para ajustarse a la [Arquitectura de Conjunto de Instrucciones](/guides/transpile#instruction-set-architecture) (ISA) del backend de destino. Este `isa_circuit` contiene dos parámetros.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"param-circuits\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3a. Migrate parameterized circuits {#step-3a-migrate-parameterized-circuits}"
msgstr "Paso 3a. Migrar circuitos parametrizados {#step-3a-migrate-parameterized-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With Sampler, parameter values are the second element of the PUB tuple. With Executor,\n"
"pass them as `circuit_arguments` to `append_circuit_item`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Con Sampler, los valores de los parámetros son el segundo elemento de la tupla PUB. Con Executor,\n"
"pásalos como `circuit_arguments` a `append_circuit_item`.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Executor**\n"
msgstr "**Executor**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"twirling\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3b. Migrate built-in twirling to explicit annotations {#step-3b-migrate-built-in-twirling-to-explicit-annotations}"
msgstr "Paso 3b. Migrar el twirling integrado a anotaciones explícitas {#step-3b-migrate-built-in-twirling-to-explicit-annotations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the most significant change. Sampler applies twirling for you by using options. With \n"
"Executor, you declare that intent explicitly by using annotated boxes and\n"
"a samplex (from [Samplomatic](/guides/directed-execution-model#samplomatic)).\n"
msgstr ""
"Este es el cambio más significativo. Sampler aplica el twirling por ti usando opciones. Con \n"
"Executor, declaras esa intención explícitamente usando cajas anotadas y\n"
"un samplex (de [Samplomatic](/guides/directed-execution-model#samplomatic)).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Sampler (twirling by using options):**\n"
msgstr "**Sampler (twirling usando opciones):**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Executor (twirling by using boxes and a samplex):**\n"
msgstr "**Executor (twirling usando cajas y un samplex):**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because the template circuit and samplex are built on the client side, you can\n"
"inspect and sample them locally to verify the output before sending anything to\n"
"hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Debido a que el circuito de plantilla y el samplex se crean en el lado del cliente, puedes\n"
"inspeccionarlos y muestrearlos localmente para verificar la salida antes de enviar nada al\n"
"hardware.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"sample-local\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verification: Sample the template circuit locally {#verification-sample-the-template-circuit-locally}"
msgstr "Verificación: Muestrear el circuito de plantilla localmente {#verification-sample-the-template-circuit-locally}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can draw randomizations from the samplex and bind them to the template\n"
"circuit to confirm that the samplex is producing the parameter values you expect.\n"
"The parameter values returned by `samplex.sample` are directly compatible with the\n"
"template circuit's parameters.\n"
msgstr ""
"Puedes extraer aleatorizaciones del samplex y vincularlas al circuito de plantilla\n"
"para confirmar que el samplex está produciendo los valores de parámetros que esperas.\n"
"Los valores de parámetros devueltos por `samplex.sample` son directamente compatibles con los\n"
"parámetros del circuito de plantilla.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To go further, you can verify that each randomization is logically equivalent to the\n"
"original circuit by, for example, converting both to `Operator` objects and comparing their unitary implementations (after\n"
"accounting for the `outputs[\"measurement_flips.<register>\"]` corrections that undo\n"
"measurement twirling), or by comparing expectation values from a local\n"
"`StatevectorSampler` or `StatevectorEstimator` run. See the Samplomatic\n"
"[Samplex inputs and outputs](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/samplex_io.html)\n"
"guide for a complete walkthrough.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para ir más allá, puedes verificar que cada aleatorización sea lógicamente equivalente al\n"
"circuito original, por ejemplo, convirtiendo ambos a objetos `Operator` y comparando sus implementaciones unitarias (después de\n"
"tener en cuenta las correcciones de `outputs[\"measurement_flips.<register>\"]` que deshacen\n"
"el twirling de medición), o comparando valores de expectativa de una ejecución local de\n"
"`StatevectorSampler` o `StatevectorEstimator`. Consulta la guía de Samplomatic\n"
"[Entradas y salidas de Samplex](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/samplex_io.html)\n"
"para ver un recorrido completo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"shots\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4. Change how shots are requested {#step-4-change-how-shots-are-requested}"
msgstr "Paso 4. Cambiar cómo se solicitan los shots {#step-4-change-how-shots-are-requested}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Move shots from the PUB to `QuantumProgram(shots=...)`.  In Executor, `shots` applies to the whole job. Submit multiple jobs if you need different shot counts.\n"
msgstr "Mueve los shots del PUB a `QuantumProgram(shots=...)`.  En Executor, `shots` se aplica a todo el trabajo. Envía varios trabajos si necesitas diferentes cantidades de shots.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"options\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 5. Update options as necessary {#step-5-update-options-as-necessary}"
msgstr "Paso 5. Actualizar las opciones según sea necesario {#step-5-update-options-as-necessary}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are fewer options available to Executor than Sampler, because\n"
"error-mitigation choices now live in your annotations and samplex instead of options.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hay menos opciones disponibles para Executor que para Sampler, porque\n"
"las decisiones de mitigación de errores ahora residen en tus anotaciones y samplex en lugar de en opciones.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is also a structural difference in where settings live. \n"
msgstr "También hay una diferencia estructural en dónde residen los ajustes. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- With Sampler,\n"
"everything, including choices that affect result post-processing, is configured on\n"
"the primitive's options or in the PUB. \n"
msgstr ""
"- Con Sampler,\n"
"todo, incluidas las decisiones que afectan el procesamiento posterior de los resultados, se configura en\n"
"las opciones de la primitiva o en el PUB. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- With Executor, choices that affect how the job\n"
"results are shaped and post-processed are set on the [`QuantumProgram`](/guides/executor-input-output#inputs-quantum-programs), not on\n"
"`ExecutorOptions`. \n"
msgstr ""
"- Con Executor, las decisiones que afectan cómo se dan forma y se procesan posteriormente los\n"
"resultados del trabajo se establecen en el [`QuantumProgram`](/guides/executor-input-output#inputs-quantum-programs), no en\n"
"`ExecutorOptions`. \n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Examples:\n"
msgstr "Examples:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Sampler      | Executor                    |\n"
"|--------------|-----------------------------|\n"
"| `shots`      | `QuantumProgram(shots=...)` |\n"
"| `meas_type` | `QuantumProgram(meas_level=...)` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Sampler      | Executor                    |\n"
"|--------------|-----------------------------|\n"
"| `shots`      | `QuantumProgram(shots=...)` |\n"
"| `meas_type` | `QuantumProgram(meas_level=...)` |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[`ExecutorOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-executor-options) holds only lower-level execution and environment\n"
"settings that don't change the structure of the returned data. It has three top-level groups:\n"
msgstr ""
"[`ExecutorOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-executor-options) contiene solo ajustes de ejecución y entorno de nivel más bajo que no cambian la estructura de los\n"
"datos devueltos. Tiene tres grupos de nivel superior:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`environment` ([`EnvironmentOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-environment-options))\n"
msgstr "`environment` ([`EnvironmentOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-environment-options))\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`execution` ([`ExecutionOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-execution-options)): Contains fewer options than with Sampler.  For example, there  is no `meas_type` Executor option. \n"
msgstr "`execution` ([`ExecutionOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-execution-options)): Contiene menos opciones que con Sampler.  Por ejemplo, no hay opción `meas_type` en Executor. \n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`experimental`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-executor-options#experimental)\n"
msgstr "[`experimental`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-executor-options#experimental)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Notably, the `twirling` and `dynamical_decoupling` options exist in Sampler but not Executor. Instead, those option values are expressed through the directed execution model.\n"
msgstr "En particular, las opciones `twirling` y `dynamical_decoupling` existen en Sampler pero no en Executor. En su lugar, esos valores de opciones se expresan a través del modelo de ejecución dirigida.\n"

